  "facts": [
    "The Sveti Rok Tunnel stretches 5.68 kilometres through the Velebit mountains, with its northern portal perched at 561 metres above sea level and the southern at 510 metres, creating a dramatic elevation drop for drivers.",
    "Built using the New Austrian Tunnelling method, the tunnel’s two tubes—25 metres apart—feature 15 foot‑high passages and an autonomous drainage system that channels water from both cleaning and seepage.",
    "Equipped with variable traffic signs and dual VHF radio frequencies (HR1 95.1 MHz, HR2 98.1 MHz), the Sveti Rok Tunnel maintains safety and communication even during peak tourist seasons to Dalmatia."
  ],
